# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What this repository publishes
#
# The editor, the tests that verify it, and the two documents a reader of the
# paper actually needs: the roadmap of known gaps and the coverage table. Those
# are named individually below.
#
# Everything else under docs/ is working material — notes, drafts, and the
# correspondence around submission. None of it is published, and the rules at
# the bottom of this file keep it that way rather than leaving it to be
# remembered.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

docs/*
# The coverage table is the probe's own output: the conclusion lives in the
# probe, and this is that conclusion in readable form. The paper's Open
# Practices statement points at it, so it has to be here.
!docs/JSPsych_TIMELINE_COVERAGE.md

# tests/ is ignored except the probe and its baseline — the safety net for the
# data-model work, which cannot be reproduced if it does not travel with the
# code.
tests/*
!tests/expvis_probe.py
!tests/golden/
# The behavioural tests: the layer the probe has no equivalent of. Same reason
# as the probe — a verification that does not travel with the code is not a
# verification.
!tests/behavior/
!tests/setup/

# The dev-only manifest the behavioural tests need. The editor itself still
# ships as index.html + js/editor.js, with no build step and no runtime
# dependencies.
!package.json
!package-lock.json
!jest.config.js
node_modules/
.DS_Store

# Word documents never enter the repository, and neither does markdown except
# where it is named. An allow-list rather than a deny-list: a new draft is
# ignored by default, so publishing one has to be a decision rather than an
# oversight.
*.docx
*.md
!README.md
# The roadmap is the paper's future-directions section, kept out of the paper
# so that it can be corrected. A published tutorial cannot be.
!ROADMAP.md
